course: dictionary
lesson: 5500
title: Words with a place: lawn
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lawn is a patch of short, neat grass, usually in a garden or park, that is cut regularly. The words around lawn often give you clues. «On a park lawn a gull may stamp its feet» tells you the lawn is outdoors, on grass.
explain: Clues can also tell you what a lawn is like. In the sentence «signs on lawns», people put signs out on the grass, so a lawn is a piece of grass that people can see. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "signs on short, neat grass" still make sense? If it does, you have it right.
explain: Other clues show what people do to a lawn. People mow it, cut it and keep off it. In «a huge furry queen bumblebee zigzags low over the lawn», the bee is flying close to the grass. When you meet a new word, ask yourself: what would I see, touch or do here?
fact: A lawn is an area of short, neat grass.
fact: Lawns are usually found in gardens or parks, and they are cut regularly.
fact: «Mow the lawn» means cut the grass, usually with a lawnmower.
fact: «Keep off the lawn» is a sign asking people not to walk on the grass.
fact: Lawnmowers are dangerous: keep well away when one is running and never touch the blades.
exercise: «On a park lawn a gull may stamp its feet up and down.» Where is the lawn? | Inside a school hall | Under the water of a pond | *On short grass in a park | On a busy motorway
exercise: «A blue or yellow ball is easier to find on a lawn.» Why is that? | Balls are heavier on grass | Dogs cannot see grass at all | *Dogs see blue and yellow well | Lawns are always painted blue
exercise: Mum says, «Please keep off the lawn, the grass is wet.» What should you do? | Lie down on the grass | Kick a ball across the lawn | *Walk on the path instead | Run across the grass
test: What is a lawn? | A deep, dark pond | A tall field of wheat | A kind of gull | *A neat patch of short grass, usually in a garden or park
test: Dad will mow the lawn on Saturday. What is Dad going to do? | Wash the car | *Cut the grass | Paint the fence | Plant a tree
exam: Ella sees a lawnmower running in the park. What should she do? | Put her hand on the blades to feel them | Stand right next to it to watch | *Keep well away from it and never touch the blades | Climb on top of it
